WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.334
Let's
begin with The Washington

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.836
Post reporting on two

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:03.803
Trump employees

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.806
allegedly moving boxes of papers at Mar

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.843
a Lago just one day before FBI

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.611
agents traveled there to pick up

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.079
classified documents.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.881
And that's not all the Post reports.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:15.849
And investigators

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:17.017
also have evidence

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.184
that the former president

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.686
kept classified documents

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.454
out in the open in his office

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.456
and showed them to others.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.524
We're going to bring in my panel.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.959
We have Errol Louis,

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.827
political anchor for Spectrum News,

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.696
also Rachel Nichols of Headliners

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.364
with Rachel Nichols on Showtime,

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.333
Republican strategist Jason Osborne

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.402
and CNN political commentator S.E. Cupp.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.237
But here first to help us break this down

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.638
legally is our CNN chief

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:39.773
legal analyst, Laura Cox.

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.741
Laura, great to see you.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:44.010
So tell me, what does all all of these

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:44.711
new developments,

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.446
what are the legal implications

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:47.514
here for Donald Trump?

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:50.450
Wow, Alisyn.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.351
I mean, just think about it.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:52.352
One of the hardest things

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.887
to do as a prosecutor

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:54.554
is to figure out

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.155
how I'm going

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:56.823
to get inside of the brain

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.324
of a potential target.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.493
How do I figure out that person's intent?

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.294
How do I figure out

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:03.263
what they really wanted to do?

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:04.697
And then you have this reporting

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.466
that suggests that not just that

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.234
the documents were retained

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.736
or that they were moved,

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:10.637
but the possibility

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.205
of even a dress rehearsal

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.040
to figure out what to do

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.443
when the National Archives

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.178
came to get the documents

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:19.512
or duly executed,

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.481
a subpoena was actually issued

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.949
and then fulfilled.

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:24.818
It really does not bode

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:27.854
well for a intended defendant or target

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:28.621
to have

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.457
this type of information out there,

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:32.492
because it really confirms

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.594
the possibility that you do have intent,

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:35.695
the intentional

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:37.530
act to try to obstruct

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.499
a lawful investigation.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:40.133
And remember,

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.134
this is all falling under

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.802
the Presidential Records Act.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.370
Alison, as you well know,

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.271
these documents

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.841
don't belong to the former president

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:48.808
Donald Trump.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.977
He had advance notice that they did not,

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.679
even if it was an inadvertent

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.280
retention of documents,

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.950
he was certainly four months on notice

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.418
that he was no longer

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.719
supposed to have them.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.020
So reporting that suggests

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.123
that there was a plan in place

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.958
in addition to his own attorney

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.126
having had to testify

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:08.027
in front of a grand jury Alisyn.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.429
And the attorney client privilege

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:10.330
being pierced

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.532
and under the crime fraud exception,

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:13.900
this does not bode

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.135
well for Donald Trump

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.202
to try to prove that

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.437
he did not have

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:18.805
the level of intent

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.141
that a prosecutor needs to show.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.376
So if this reporting bears out

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:24.811
and we've heard bits

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.613
and pieces of this before

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:27.680
and Jeff Smith

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.015
the special counsel, has evidence

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:31.417
of this, does Merrick Garland charge

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:32.218
Donald Trump

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.321
Well, remember, he is not

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:36.723
the first one to make the call.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:37.590
It would be the person

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.558
that he has given

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:39.993
and delegated the responsibility

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.694
to Jack Smith, in part

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.596
because of the political implications

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:44.030
here.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.632
Obviously, Donald Trump

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.133
is the presumed frontrunner

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.501
in the GOP primary.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.969
He's a former president.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.939
He has made no small news about the idea

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:53.640
that he believes

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.109
all of this is a perpetual witch hunt.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:56.709
And so

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.845
there is a distant ten foot pole

00:02:58.845 --> 00:02:59.579
that Merrick Garland

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.347
wants to have between himself

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:02.248
for obvious reasons,

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.449
a political appointee,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.984
the head of the executive branch

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.753
under the pleasure of President Biden,

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:09.489
the chief rival of the GOP primary lead.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:10.290
And, of course,

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.325
what's happening in this investigation.

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.860
But if Jack Smith,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.662
who has had the delegated authority

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:16.996
to make the decision,

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:20.400
makes that determination, it really binds

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.301
Merrick Garland

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:23.703
as the AG to make a decision

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:24.537
based on what

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:25.205
the evidence

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:26.839
shows under the special counsel

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.408
whose job it is to look at this.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:29.042
And so

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.710
it is very likely in a case

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:31.311
where there is not

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.812
a whole lot of ambiguity

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:33.913
unlike some other case

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.048
that might be brewing.

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:36.883
If there's zero ambiguity

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.718
and the evidence is there.

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:39.519
Merrick Garland

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:41.087
will likely have to follow

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:43.556
the guidance of Jack Smith, whatever

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:44.457
it might be.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:47.894
Okay.
And the two staffers who reportedly moved

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:50.630
these boxes of documents.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:52.198
Are they in trouble?

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:55.235
Could be.

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:56.336
I mean, we've never seen

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:57.837
I haven't seen the photograph

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.439
you have of Donald Trump actually

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:01.274
carrying boxes anywhere.

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:02.008
I haven't seen them

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.243
carrying the documents

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.510
or to have some indication

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.713
that he himself was alone in this.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.781
If he delegated responsibility

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.083
to somebody else,

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.252
if that person was involved

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.253
played in this,

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.622
then there is the potential liability

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.690
and potential prosecution.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.292
However, think about

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.326
there might be people

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.794
who are voluntarily

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.763
or actively cooperating

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:26.132
to give the information to convey

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:27.100
that there is likely

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.201
that there was a dress rehearsal

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:28.968
or otherwise.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.703
And I point again to Evan Corcoran.

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.171
Remember, he was the attorney

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:33.273
for Donald Trump.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:34.374
He tried to suggest

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:35.742
he could not tell

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:37.910
what may have been instructed to him

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.812
or otherwise because of obviously

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.648
the attorney client privilege we want.

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:44.017
Amy client to be able to be fully

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:46.252
forthright and to

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.820
be candid with their counsel,

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.322
to get legal advice.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.323
And we will shield

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:51.891
those communications, Alisyn.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.726
Except if there is a crime

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.061
or fraud afoot.

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:55.528
And yes,

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:57.597
I said a foot on a Thursday night

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:58.898
at 10:00 p.m.,

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.867
but really, if there was a crime afoot

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:02.168
and fraud happening,

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:03.469
we don't want to protect that.

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.404
We don't want to use

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:05.705
a shield of an attorney

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:06.806
to further a crime.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:09.008
And so a judge has already said

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:10.510
you're going to have to testify

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:12.178
about what you may have been instructed

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:13.446
to in front of a grand jury.

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:14.047
And so

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:16.516
he apparently had very detailed notes,

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:17.216
whatever

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.084
it wasn't

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.752
contained in that secret

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:21.120
grand jury proceeding.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.355
Well, give us more insight

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:25.358
as to who else might be liable

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.527
or at least potentially

00:05:27.527 --> 00:05:28.928
having the prosecution.

00:05:28.928 --> 00:05:30.363
It sounds like something is afoot.

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:31.731
Maybe even two feet.

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:33.466
So thank you very much.

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:34.300
I knew you were going to say it.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.335
I knew it, Alisyn.

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:36.169
I didn't say

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:36.969
you knew that

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.204
I was going to say something

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:39.839
crazy right there.

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.307
I was right there with you.

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:42.375
Yeah. Tastic.

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:42.975
Great to see you.

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:44.911
Thank you very much for all of that.

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:45.378
Okay, let's

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:48.314
ask you to go back to the veil, Errol.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:51.384
The idea that the boxing guys were moved

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:54.420
after they knew the FBI was coming.

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:56.089
Okay.
They knew that

00:05:56.089 --> 00:05:57.924
they were being subpoenaed for this.

00:05:57.924 --> 00:05:59.392
And furthermore,

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:01.561
that he kept some of these

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:02.729
I mean, obviously, they have evidence

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:03.629
or they have sources to say

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:04.697
that he kept

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.099
some of these documents in the open

00:06:06.099 --> 00:06:07.433
and showed them to people.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:10.837
You'll remember in the CNN town hall

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:13.005
that he was asked about this

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:13.773
by Kaitlan Collins,

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:17.110
and his answer was a little peculiar.

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:19.078
So let me just play that for everyone.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:21.147
When it comes

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:22.048
to your documents,

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:22.982
did you ever show those

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.917
classified documents to anyone?

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:25.618
Not really.

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:26.853
I would have the right to.

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:27.220
By the way,

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.455
they would be mystified after.

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.891
Not that I can think of

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:33.793
Oh, that sounds like

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.628
the kind of thing you say under oath.

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:37.630
This is Donald Trump

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:38.631
during that town hall

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:39.665
and in other settings

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:40.400
has been trying out

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.167
every defense

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:43.603
that you know comes to mind.

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:44.837
I can automatically do it

00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:47.106
just by an act of my mind.

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:49.742
I didn't really show it to anybody.

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:50.810
Not really.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:51.677
I don't remember

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:53.913
I could if I could if I wanted to.

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:54.614
Right.

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:57.116
He often has this habit of doing things

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:58.351
in the open

00:06:58.351 --> 00:06:58.985
and try

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:00.686
trying to inoculate those actions

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:01.888
by saying clearly,

00:07:01.888 --> 00:07:03.656
I wasn't trying to deceive anybody.

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:04.724
I just laid it out there

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:05.992
and everybody could see the boxes.

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:06.659
That was something else,

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:07.860
he said during the town hall.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.362
Everybody saw the boxes.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:10.530
What are you talking about?

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.331
I'm not trying to do anything

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:14.600
that's improper or illegal.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.369
So the problem for him,

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:17.403
of course, is that

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.172
that doesn't really comport with the law.

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:21.174
When the National Archives

00:07:21.174 --> 00:07:22.275
comes and ask, or

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:23.876
when a subpoena is executed

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:25.578
and the Justice Department shows up,

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:27.079
you are supposed to cooperate,

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:29.081
and the noncooperation itself

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:31.017
gives rise to an offense

00:07:31.017 --> 00:07:32.485
so that even if everything

00:07:32.485 --> 00:07:33.152
he said was true,

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:33.853
if he thought he could

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:36.422
magically, mentally declassify things,

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:38.891
once the DOJ comes and says

00:07:39.559 --> 00:07:40.593
we have a subpoena

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:42.428
you have to give this stuff back

00:07:42.428 --> 00:07:43.529
and you don't do it,

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:45.031
or you have a rehearsal

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:45.932
just to sort of pretend

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:47.400
that you're going to do it.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.601
You get into a lot of trouble.

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:49.335
And I think he's

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:50.169
heading for a lot of legal

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:51.003
trouble, right?

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:52.972
So the obstruction is one thing.

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:54.340
And by the way, news at 11.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:55.875
Donald Trump does not have respect

00:07:55.875 --> 00:07:57.343
for American laws or procedure.

00:07:57.343 --> 00:07:59.145
I mean, we already knew that. So.

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:00.313
Can they prove obstruction?

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:01.380
Can they prove intent with

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.482
this new information?

00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:02.882
Maybe.

00:08:02.882 --> 00:08:03.716
It certainly looks like it

00:08:03.716 --> 00:08:04.317
from the outside.

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:04.884
We'll have to see

00:08:04.884 --> 00:08:06.752
what the legal process bears out.

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:07.620
To me, it's

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.489
the showing people of these documents

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:10.957
that really just sort of erupts

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:11.824
red flags for me.

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:13.125
We are talking about documents

00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:15.161
that have been reported as nuclear codes,

00:08:15.361 --> 00:08:17.163
national security, about operations

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:18.865
that even our top national operatives

00:08:18.865 --> 00:08:19.532
don't know about.

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:20.633
That's how secure

00:08:20.633 --> 00:08:22.335
these overseas operations are.

00:08:22.335 --> 00:08:23.703
And he's just showing them

00:08:23.703 --> 00:08:24.203
to business

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:25.171
associates and friends

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:26.606
what to feed his own ego

00:08:26.606 --> 00:08:28.541
so he can say how important he is

00:08:28.541 --> 00:08:29.408
that to me

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:30.743
is where the American electorate

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:32.378
needs to really pay attention

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:33.946
because it's not about the charges

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:35.248
or is it this legal case

00:08:35.248 --> 00:08:36.282
or that legal case?

00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:38.518
He is being reckless with American lives.

00:08:38.518 --> 00:08:39.785
That's just the bottom line,

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:40.887
whether he thought he was allowed

00:08:40.887 --> 00:08:41.954
to or not.

00:08:41.954 --> 00:08:42.421
You look at

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:43.289
what's in front of you

00:08:43.289 --> 00:08:44.524
and you show people

00:08:44.524 --> 00:08:45.324
and that's something

00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:46.659
that can get people killed.

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:47.326
And what happens

00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:48.828
if he gets back into office

00:08:48.828 --> 00:08:50.329
and he is that reckless

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:51.564
on behalf of his ego,

00:08:51.564 --> 00:08:53.165
which is just not a hard leap

00:08:53.165 --> 00:08:54.500
to think that that might happen again.

